    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW25xjkSizeFBrzHTULVxNtCU)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on current `main`; independent of the other open PRs.\n- Touches only `sp-agenda-views.el` (via `docs/tangles/text/sp-org-agenda.org`) and its inline test.\n\n## What I found\n\n- The inline keyword agenda is view `x` (`C-c o x`) in `sp-agenda-views`, from #395: an Org search view built from `sp-agenda-views-inline-keywords`.\n- That option is the only place the keyword list is defined. No font-lock, capture template or completion code reads it, so nothing else needed changing.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Filter:\n  - New `sp-agenda-views-inline-filter` (default `nil` = all keywords, so the unfiltered view stays the default).\n  - `M-x sp-agenda-views-inline-filter-set` asks for one keyword (completion over `sp-agenda-views-inline-keywords`), narrows the view and opens it.\n  - `M-x sp-agenda-views-inline-filter-clear` shows all keywords again.\n  - Transient `sp-agenda-views-inline-menu` on `C-c o X`: `x` open, `f` filter, `c` clear; its title shows the current filter.\n  - The view header names the keyword while filtered.\n  - The filter is not saved between sessions.\n- `SOURCEREFS` added to `sp-agenda-views-inline-keywords`: references made in the PDF being read, for which a litnote is being written. It is separate from `CITE`.\n- Docs: bullets in `sp-org-agenda.org` (\"Inline keyword view\", key table, PR list), `.el` edited by hand to match the blocks.\n- Tests: `tests/sp-agenda-views-inline-test.el` covers SOURCEREFS, filter on/off, unknown filter, clear.\n- `CHANGELOG.org` not edited.\n\n## What is not verified\n\n- No Emacs in the container: nothing was run, and the `.el` was not re-tangled (edited in step with the `.org`). Please run `tools/check-tangle.sh` and the test file.\n- Completion offers the configured keywords, not only those currently present in your files.\n- `customize` changes to `sp-agenda-views-inline-keywords` keep working; if you already customised that option, add `SOURCEREFS` yourself, because the new default does not apply.\n\n## Open questions\n\n- Should `SOURCEREFS` get a capture from a DEVONthink selection or a litnote template (e.g. `SOURCEREFS @citekey` linked to `#+reference:`)? Left out of this first version.\n- Should the filter also be settable from inside the agenda buffer (e.g. a key there)? Now only via `C-c o X`.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] `tools/check-tangle.sh` reports no new drift for `sp-agenda-views.el`\n- [x] `emacs -Q --batch -l ert -l tests/sp-agenda-views-inline-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` passes\n- [ ] Restart Emacs; `C-c o x` still shows every keyword's entries as before\n- [ ] Put `SOURCEREFS Smith 1999` in a draft or agenda note; `C-c o x` lists it\n- [ ] `C-c o X` opens the menu with \"filter: none\"; `f`, pick `SOURCEREFS` (completion works): the view lists only SOURCEREFS entries, header says so\n- [ ] `C-c o X`, `f`, pick `FIXME`: only FIXME entries\n- [ ] `C-c o X`, `c`: all keywords again, header back to the original\n- [ ] Typing a word that is not in the list at the `f` prompt is refused\n- [ ] Regression: other agenda views (`C-c o a SPC`, `c`, `i i`) still open\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9taQEBJAWpQmkyfLY)_",
